# `all` is a number or a text, so it comes round in a box. A read of the slot is shown to hold what the doors at its stores let in. The parameter that stands for the read is shown to hold the same: every edge into the head hands over what is shown to, or what has passed the door at its store and stands under an AssumeType, or a read.
# So the sum made of it is shown to fit the slot, as it was when the operand was read, and no door stands at the store of a turn.
